# PROBE all-values. A ⊑ ∃r.B and A ⊑ ∀r.C, with B and C disjoint, make A unsatisfiable.
# construct: ObjectAllValuesFrom
# expect: unsat :A
# expect-not: unsat :B

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:B owl:disjointWith :C .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:allValuesFrom :C ] .
